      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Mangiferin is a highly polar xanthone C-glucoside with four phenolic OH groups and a glucose moiety. The closest analog, orientin, failed to achieve meaningful brain exposure due to high polarity, while the more permeable isovitexin is less polar. Distant glycoside positives do not outweigh the close orientin evidence, so meaningful CNS access is not adequately supported.",
